# Reference for every setting. Copy to .env.local, .env.development or
# .env.staging and fill in; APP_ENV=<local|development|staging> (default local)
# picks the file (ENV_FILE=<file> overrides). scripts/env.sh reads it for every
# script, connector config (scripts/render-config.sh) and tests/test_cdc.py, and
# fills in the defaults shown. One VAR=value per line, no quotes, no comments
# after values. A variable set in the shell wins over the file.

# ---- Required: admin passwords (SQL Server MSSQL_ADMIN_USER, PostgreSQL PG_ADMIN_USER)
MSSQL_PASSWORD=change_me
PG_PASSWORD=change_me

# ---- Databases, as reached from this machine (setup-db.sh, tests)
# MSSQL_HOST=localhost
# MSSQL_PORT=1433
# MSSQL_DB=bpjsk_poc
# PG_HOST=localhost
# PG_PORT=5432
# PG_DB=bpjsk_poc

# ---- Databases, as reached from the Kafka Connect worker. Default: MSSQL_HOST /
# MSSQL_PORT (PG_*) when those are set here, else the docker-compose service
# names sqlserver:1433 / postgres:5432.
# CONNECT_MSSQL_HOST=
# CONNECT_MSSQL_PORT=
# CONNECT_PG_HOST=
# CONNECT_PG_PORT=
# Broker for the SQL Server source's schema history, as the worker reaches it.
# CONNECT_KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP=kafka:29092

# ---- Logins
# Admins: create the schema, CDC, triggers and logins (setup-db.sh); the tests write as them.
# MSSQL_ADMIN_USER=sa
# PG_ADMIN_USER=postgres
# Debezium sources. The PostgreSQL one needs REPLICATION. Passwords default to
# MSSQL_PASSWORD / PG_PASSWORD.
# MSSQL_USER=sa
# MSSQL_USER_PASSWORD=
# PG_USER=debezium_replication
# PG_USER_PASSWORD=
# JDBC sinks (setup-db.sh creates them). The loop filter drops every change
# these logins write, so nothing else may use them; must differ from the admins
# (and, for PostgreSQL, from PG_USER). Passwords default to MSSQL_PASSWORD /
# PG_PASSWORD and must not contain a single quote.
# MSSQL_SINK_USER=cdc_sink
# MSSQL_SINK_PASSWORD=
# PG_SINK_USER=cdc_sink
# PG_SINK_PASSWORD=
# Where the sinks write; defaults to the source databases above.
# MSSQL_SINK_HOST=
# MSSQL_SINK_PORT=
# MSSQL_SINK_DB=
# PG_SINK_HOST=
# PG_SINK_PORT=
# PG_SINK_DB=

# ---- Endpoints (user/password optional, for basic auth)
# CONNECT_URL=http://localhost:8083
# CONNECT_USER=
# CONNECT_PWD=
# KSQLDB_URL=http://localhost:8088
# KSQLDB_USER=
# KSQLDB_PASSWORD=
# inline: passwords are written into the connector configs (readable by anyone
# with access to the Connect REST API). worker: configs keep ${env:...} and the
# Connect worker must have those variables (the local compose sets them).
# CONNECT_SECRETS=inline
# Broker as reached from this machine (tests only).
# KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP=localhost:9092

# ---- Example: development (see .env.development)
# MSSQL_HOST=sqlserver.kodehive.id
# MSSQL_PORT=6978
# PG_HOST=postgres.kodehive.id
# PG_PORT=6969
# PG_ADMIN_USER=developer
# CONNECT_URL=https://connect.kafka.kodehive.id
# CONNECT_USER=<connect user>
# CONNECT_PWD=<connect password>
# KSQLDB_URL=https://ksqldb.kafka.kodehive.id
# KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP=kafka.kodehive.id:9092
